    "show_share": true,
    "description": "In an exciting collaboration with the Academy of Sciences of Lisbon, the Aga Khan University (International) in the United Kingdom concluded a four-day summer short course on Arabic Manuscripts, Codicology, and Philology, which was organised from 8 to 11 July in Lisbon's magnificent Academy of Sciences building. The opening day was graced by esteemed guests, including Nazim Ahmad, Diplomatic Representative of the Delegation of the Ismaili Imamat in Portugal; José Luís Cardoso, President of the Academy of Sciences; Professor Henrique Leitão, Inspector of the ACL Library, Mr Rahim Kassam, the Executive Director of the Delegation, and Ms Susana Ramos, Special Projects Manager from the AKDN office in Lisbon.",
